- entry .Intersectable   set algebra over an abstract receiver: `intersect` and `except`
+ entry .Intersectable   álgebra de conjuntos sobre un receptor abstracto: `intersect` y `except`

= entry .Intersectable   set algebra over an abstract receiver: `intersect` and `except`
-   detail
+   detail

-       `left.intersect(right)` keeps the elements present in both and `left.except(right)`
-       removes `right`'s elements (the standard library's `diff`). Union is not here: for an
-       unordered unique shape it is plain concatenation, which symbolism's `Concatenable`
-       already provides as `left + right`, and a single element is added with `:+`.
+       `left.intersect(right)` conserva los elementos presentes en ambos y `left.except(right)`
+       elimina los elementos de `right` (el `diff` de la biblioteca estándar). La unión no está
+       aquí: para una forma de elementos únicos sin orden es una simple concatenación, que el
+       `Concatenable` de symbolism ya proporciona como `left + right`, y un solo elemento se
+       añade con `:+`.

=       already provides as `left + right`, and a single element is added with `:+`.
=
-       ```scala
+       ```scala

=       already provides as `left + right`, and a single element is added with `:+`.
=
=       ```scala
-       import soundness.*
+       import soundness.*

-       val primes = Set(2, 3, 5, 7)
+       val primes = Set(2, 3, 5, 7)

-       primes.intersect(Set(2, 4))   // Set(2)
+       primes.intersect(Set(2, 4))   // Set(2)

-       primes.except(Set(2, 3))      // Set(5, 7)
+       primes.except(Set(2, 3))      // Set(5, 7)

-       primes :+ 11                  // Set(2, 3, 5, 7, 11)
+       primes :+ 11                  // Set(2, 3, 5, 7, 11)

=       primes :+ 11                  // Set(2, 3, 5, 7, 11)
-       ```
+       ```

-       The one instance, `.set`, is deliberately not subtype-parametric: an intersection can
-       empty a non-empty receiver, so a `& Populated` brand must not survive it.
+       La única instancia, `.set`, deliberadamente no es paramétrica en el subtipo: una
+       intersección puede vaciar un receptor no vacío, así que una marca `& Populated` no debe
+       sobrevivir a ella.

